window.mutagenWiki = [{"title":"Player controls","page":"Controls and commands","url":"commands.html#keys","text":"Key Action G Open the Gene Tree N Toggle creature vision R Use the stage II ability V Use the stage III ability B Use the apex ability"},{"title":"Operator commands","page":"Controls and commands","url":"commands.html#commands","text":"The command group requires permission level 2. Strains accept an ID such as mutagen:zombie or the short name zombie . Brackets enclose optional arguments. Command Action /mutagen status [target] Show strain, progress and other state. /mutagen list List available strains. /mutagen dose <strain> [quality] Add a dose while bypassing the normal research cap. Quality ranges from 1 to 100. /mutagen set <strain> <progress> Set transformation progress from 0 to 100. /mutagen lock <true|false> Enable or disable the progress lock. /mutagen clear Clear active strains. /mutagen research Show research progress. /mutagen research <strain> <percent> Set research for a strain. /mutagen abilities Show the active abilities and cooldowns. /mutagen use <index> Try to activate an ability by index."},{"title":"Make a strain","page":"Datapacks","url":"datapacks.html#start","text":"Create a datapack in the world’s datapacks folder with a pack.mcmeta for Minecraft 1.21.1. Place a strain at data/<namespace>/mutagen/strains/<name>.json . Run /reload and look for the strain in /mutagen list . If the file is skipped, check the server log. Server datapacks sync to players. Everyone still needs the same build of Mutagen. {\"entity\":\"minecraft:witch\",\"color\":\"#6A2C8C\",\"difficulty\":2}"},{"title":"Strain, body and vision fields","page":"Datapacks","url":"datapacks.html#fields","text":"Field Required Default What it is entity yes The mob this strain comes from. One strain per mob color no #7FAE6B \"#RRGGBB\" or a number. Used for the HUD, particles and, with skin: color , the infection scale no 1.0 Render scale in full form difficulty no 1 1–10. Harder species take longer to sequence synthesis no catalyst (item, default: Mutagen's catalyst), catalyst_count (1–64, default 1), time in ticks (default 300) body no How the body changes, see below traits no [] Passive traits, see below abilities no [] Active abilities, see below. Order matters vision no Creature vision, see below Field Default What it is model_layer <entity>#main Which vanilla model layer to take parts from, e.g. \"minecraft:zombie\" or \"minecraft:drowned#outer\" parts matched by name Which part of the mob each player bone becomes. Each entry: part (path in the model, like \"head\" or \"body/tail\" ), bone (player bone), grow ( true for parts a human doesn't have, like tails), scale ( [x, y, z] ) absorb [] Player bones that should melt into the torso. Bones with no matching part do this automatically spread right arm, body, left arm, head, legs The order bones start changing and the skin spreads skin color Only for the first-person hand and the older method: texture takes infection colours from the mob's texture (player-shaped textures only), color uses the strain colour morph [] Extra posture: bone and rotation in degrees width , height , eye_height the mob's own Hitbox and eye height in full form reach 0 Extra reach in blocks in full form (can be negative) overlays [] Extra layers drawn on the hybrid: texture , optional model_layer , emissive for glowing eyes Field Default What it is shader A post-effect chain, e.g. \"minecraft:shaders/post/creeper.json\" , or your own from a resource pack from_stage manifestation When the vision starts. It gets stronger with progress and is full at 100%"},{"title":"Trait types","page":"Datapacks","url":"datapacks.html#traits","text":"Type Fields What it does attribute attribute , amount , operation ( add_value / add_multiplied_base / add_multiplied_total ) Any attribute: health, speed, damage, armour, step height, gravity, swim speed… Negative amounts are fine effect_immunity effects Immune to these effects damage_factor damage_type (damage type tag, e.g. \"#minecraft:is_fire\" ), factor Multiplies incoming damage. 0 = immune, above 1 = weakness dark_regeneration amplifier , max_light Regeneration in the dark permanent_effect effect , amplifier An effect that's always on dark_effect effect , amplifier , max_light An effect that's on only in the dark water_effect effect , amplifier An effect that's on only in water arrow_power factor Your arrows hit harder mob_neutrality kin (entity tag) and/or entities These mobs stop targeting you wall_climb Climb walls like a spider web_walker Cobwebs don't slow you thorns damage Hurts anyone who hits you in melee on_hit_effect effect , duration , amplifier , self_damage Your melee hits apply an effect; can cost you health growth_aura radius , tries Crops and saplings nearby grow faster flight speed , exhaustion , min_food , rain Creative-style flight. Costs hunger; stops below min_food , and in rain/water if rain is false aquatic_body Fast, buoyant swimming, gills and clear underwater vision Type Fields What it does sun_burn Burns in daylight without a helmet water_damage amount , rain Water (and rain) hurts dry_out grace (seconds), amount Weakens, then gets hurt after too long out of water water_dependence Breathes only in water; hops and sees poorly on land cat_fear radius Panics near cats and ocelots fear entities , radius Panics near these mobs homesick dimension , effects Gets these effects outside its home dimension hoard items (item tag) Can't throw these items away diet foods (item tag) Eats only these foods no_eating food_level Doesn't eat at all; hunger stays at food_level no_sleep Can't sleep armor_rejection slots (default: all four) Can't wear armour in these slots no_offhand No off-hand no_tools Can't hold anything in mutagen:needs_hands no_crafting stations (block tag), grid Can't use these stations; with grid , not even the inventory crafting grid no_building Can't place blocks (doors, chests and levers still work) inventory_limit hotbar Only this many hotbar slots; the rest of the inventory is locked"},{"title":"Ability types","page":"Datapacks","url":"datapacks.html#abilities","text":"Field Default What it is type One of the types below from_stage When it unlocks name Shown in the HUD and gene tree cooldown 200 In ticks cost free hunger and/or health . Saturation goes first; health never takes the last heart apex false The B ability requires any water , dry , airborne , ground , nether or dark Type Fields What it does effect_burst effects , duration , amplifier Gives you effects leap power , lift , effects , duration , amplifier Jumps where you look; optional effects after shockwave radius , damage , knockback , ignite Hits and pushes everything around you volley arrows , spread , velocity , damage Fires a fan of arrows that can't be picked up fireball count , spread Fires small fireballs hex range or radius , damage , effects , duration , amplifier , particle , sound Magic hit on the target you're looking at, or on everyone around you if radius is set vortex radius , pull , damage , duration Pulls everyone in and slows them lunge range , power , damage Throws you at the target; hits on contact blink range , effects , duration Teleports to a safe spot where you're looking reveal radius , duration Makes living things around you glow through walls rally kin (entity tag) and/or entities , radius , duration Turns nearby mobs on whoever last hurt you. Nothing is spawned"},{"title":"Examples and troubleshooting","page":"Datapacks","url":"datapacks.html#examples","text":"To replace a built-in strain, use its original file path under data/mutagen/mutagen/strains/ . For custom names and descriptions you can use translations from a resource pack. See the full datapack specification for model mapping, vision effects and working examples."},{"title":"Lab equipment","page":"Lab and research","url":"lab.html#equipment","text":"Machine What it does Bio Workbench Opens a recipe list and lays out ingredients from your inventory when you select a recipe. Sequencer Consumes a sample and redstone to advance research for that species. Centrifuge Uses furnace fuel to refine a raw sample into a genome in about ten seconds. Synthesizer Combines a purified genome with mutagen base and a catalyst. A genome with at least 85% purity normally yields two ampoules."},{"title":"Research thresholds","page":"Lab and research","url":"lab.html#research","text":"Research Unlock 25% View the genes and make serum capped at 40% transformation. 50% Make serum capped at 70%. 75% Make serum that can reach full form. 100% The strain holds without a stabilizer and can use its apex ability at full form."},{"title":"Samples and catalysts","page":"Lab and research","url":"lab.html#sampling","text":"Use a syringe on the mob in Minecraft. Sample quality matters: adult or weakened targets tend to give better samples, and spawner mobs give poorer ones. Golden and netherite syringes improve sample quality. Some strains use a catalyst specific to that mob. Press G to see the strains you have sampled and their research progress. Mutagen shares research across the world by default."},{"title":"Bio Workbench","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#bio_workbench","text":"Crafting Table  3 × Glass 5 × Iron Ingot 1 × Crafting Table"},{"title":"Carrier Fluid","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#carrier_fluid","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Potion 1 × Sugar 1 × Slimeball"},{"title":"Catalyst","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#catalyst","text":"Bio Workbench · ×2  1 × Nether Wart 1 × Nether Quartz"},{"title":"Centrifuge","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#centrifuge","text":"Bio Workbench  5 × Iron Ingot 2 × Glass 1 × Redstone Dust 1 × Furnace"},{"title":"Golden Syringe","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#golden_syringe","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Syringe 3 × Gold Ingot 1 × Redstone Dust"},{"title":"Mutagen Base","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#mutagen_base","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Carrier Fluid 1 × Bottle o' Enchanting"},{"title":"Netherite Syringe","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#netherite_syringe","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Golden Syringe 2 × Netherite Scrap"},{"title":"Reversal Serum","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#reversal_serum","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Carrier Fluid 1 × Fermented Spider Eye"},{"title":"Sequencer","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#sequencer","text":"Bio Workbench  4 × Iron Ingot 2 × Glass 1 × Redstone Comparator 1 × Spyglass"},{"title":"Stabilizer","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#stabilizer","text":"Bio Workbench  1 × Carrier Fluid 1 × Glowstone Dust"},{"title":"Synthesizer","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#synthesizer","text":"Bio Workbench  4 × Iron Ingot 3 × Glass 1 × Brewing Stand 1 × Redstone Dust"},{"title":"Syringe","page":"Blocks and recipes","url":"recipes.html#syringe","text":"Bio Workbench · ×2  1 × Glass Bottle 1 × Iron Ingot 1 × Iron Nugget"},{"title":"Configuration file","page":"Server configuration","url":"server.html#config","text":"Find the settings in config/mutagen.json . Set knowledgeScope to player for separate research per player. humanityPenalties controls restrictions such as losing the use of tools in handless forms."},{"title":"Default values","page":"Server configuration","url":"server.html#defaults","text":"Key Default What it does transformationSpeed 1.0 How fast doses absorb and wear off doseStrength 20.0 How much one 100%-purity dose adds humanityPenalties true Losing hands, armour and so on sunlightBurn true Undead strains burning in daylight hud true Shows the strain panel hudCorner top_left Panel position: top_left , top_right , bottom_right , bottom_left fullFormRender true Draw you as the actual mob at stage V maxGenes 1 How many strains one body can hold. Chimeras come later knowledgeScope world world : everyone shares research. player : each player has their own researchSpeed 1.0 How much each sequencer run teaches you doubleSerumPurity 85.0 Genome purity for two ampoules per synthesis; 101 turns it off hybridRender true The creature's parts on your body at stages II–IV bodyMorph true Your proportions and posture change bodyMotion true Convulsions between stages and twitching later on pehkuiIntegration true Use Pehkui for body size if it's installed mobVision false Creature vision. Also toggled with N"},{"title":"Compatibility","page":"Server configuration","url":"server.html#compatibility","text":"Mod Notes Pehkui Handles body size if installed. Turn off with pehkuiIntegration Sodium / Embeddium Works fine Iris / Oculus Works; mutation overlays skip the shadow pass Skin and cape mods Your skin is whatever they give you. The cape disappears in full form Figura Your avatar might cover the hybrid or the full form. Turn off hybridRender / fullFormRender if they fight"},{"title":"Install Mutagen","page":"Installation and quick start","url":"start.html#install","text":"Use Minecraft Java Edition 1.21.1, Java 21, and a Fabric or NeoForge profile. Choose the matching build on the versions page . Add Architectury API and GeckoLib . Fabric also requires Fabric API . Put the files in the profile’s mods folder. For multiplayer, the server and players need the same Mutagen build."},{"title":"Your first transformation","page":"Installation and quick start","url":"start.html#first-run","text":"Craft a Bio Workbench and make the lab equipment there. Collect a sample from a mob and use the Sequencer to study its strain. Purify a sample in the Centrifuge, then use the Synthesizer to make serum. Use the serum in Minecraft and watch the progress bar in the strain panel. See Transformation for the stages and reversal."},{"title":"Troubleshooting","page":"Installation and quick start","url":"start.html#troubleshooting","text":"Check that the mod, dependencies and loader target Minecraft 1.21.1 and that there is only one Mutagen build in mods . If the game crashes, look in logs/latest.log . Include your loader and mod versions in a bug report."},{"title":"Strengths and weaknesses","page":"Strains and abilities","url":"strains.html#comparison","text":"Strain The good The bad Zombie More health, armour and damage, regenerates in the dark, immune to Hunger 12% slower, burns in the sun, can't sleep; meat only in full form Skeleton Stronger arrows, night vision, immune to poison and Hunger, softer falls Less health, explosions hurt more, burns in the sun, can't sleep Creeper Takes less from explosions, faster, extra armour, creepers leave you alone Scared of cats, fire hurts more Spider Climbs walls, walks through cobwebs, jumps higher, sees in the dark Fire hurts more, can't wear a helmet from stage IV Enderman Steps over full blocks, more health and damage, arrows hit you less Water and rain burn Drowned Swims fast, breathes and sees underwater Slow on land, burns in the sun; in full form it dries out after three minutes away from water Blaze Fire can't hurt you from stage III, flies from stage IV, softer falls Water and rain burn and ground you, arrows hurt more Phantom Light body, night vision, the fastest flyer from stage IV Less health, burns in the sun, no chestplate over the wings Bee Crops grow faster around you, flies from stage IV, barely feels a fall Less health, sweet food only, rain grounds you Wolf Faster, bites harder, raw and rotten meat is fine Meat only, scared of llamas, fire hurts more Piglin Piglins treat you as one of them, no gold needed. Fire hurts less, more health and damage Can't throw away anything gold, scared of zombies and zombified piglins, weaker outside the Nether in full form Guardian Swims fast and floats, gills, clear underwater vision, spikes that hurt attackers, more armour and health Hops slowly on land, can't see well there, and from stage IV runs out of air out of water"},{"title":"Ability keys and costs","page":"Strains and abilities","url":"strains.html#ability-keys","text":"R unlocks at stage II, V at stage III. The apex ability on B needs full form and 100% research. The HUD shows cooldowns and unmet conditions. A failed attempt spends nothing. Blaze, phantom, and bee can fly from stage IV by double-tapping jump. Flight uses hunger, and rain or water grounds them."},{"title":"Abilities by strain","page":"Strains and abilities","url":"strains.html#ability-list","text":"Strain R V B (apex) Zombie Dead Flesh: quick regeneration and resistance Ground Slam: hits everyone around you The Horde: nearby zombies go after whoever hurt you Skeleton Dead Eye: see living things through walls Volley: three arrows Arrow Storm: nine arrows Creeper Pressure Release: pushes everyone back Camouflage: a few seconds of invisibility Detonation: a big blast that costs you 4 HP and leaves blocks alone Spider Pounce: leap forward Venom Spit: poison a target Cocoon: slows and weakens a target Enderman Blink: teleport where you're looking Void Stare: slows and weakens a target Void Collapse: pulls everyone in and slows them Drowned Water Surge: dash underwater Undertow: pulls everyone in The Tide: damages and slows everyone around Blaze Fireball Fire Salvo: three fireballs Inferno: sets everyone around on fire Phantom Wingbeat: jump up and glide down Night Veil: invisibility in the dark Dive: dive-bomb a target from the air Bee Wingbeat: jump up and float down Sting: poison, costs half a heart The Swarm: nearby bees go after whoever hurt you Wolf Scent: see living things through walls Leaping Bite: jump at a target and bite The Pack: nearby wolves go after whoever hurt you Piglin Fury: strength and speed Charge: rush a target Warband: nearby piglins join in (Nether only) Guardian Sonar: see living things through walls Beam: a laser hit from range Elder Curse: slows and weakens everyone around"},{"title":"Progress and decay","page":"Transformation","url":"transformation.html#progress","text":"An in-game serum dose fills an absorption reserve. Progress rises as the reserve is used and can fall again when it runs out. Full form is permanent until reversed."},{"title":"The five stages","page":"Transformation","url":"transformation.html#stages","text":"Stage Progress What happens I. Infection 1–20% Nothing you can see yet, apart from a few particles and the first passive trait II. Manifestation 21–40% Patches of the creature start showing on your skin. First ability III. Mutation 41–70% Your body starts changing shape. Second ability IV. Domination 71–99% You're more creature than human. Flyers can fly, handless bodies lose the off-hand V. Full Form 100% You are the creature. This stage doesn't wear off"},{"title":"Stabilize or reverse","page":"Transformation","url":"transformation.html#control","text":"Use a stabilizer to hold the current level. Use it again to release the lock. A reversal serum rolls progress back by 15 percentage points per dose and applies nausea, weakness and damage. At later stages the body shape, hitbox and camera height follow the creature. fullFormRender controls the creature renderer at 100%."}];
